   "html": "<p>The most common commands. The keys are the defaults; you can remap them (see <strong>Controls</strong>). The game never uses browser shortcuts such as F5 or Ctrl with a number.</p><div class=\"help-table\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\"><strong>To...</strong></th><th scope=\"col\"><strong>Mouse</strong></th><th scope=\"col\"><strong>Touch</strong></th><th scope=\"col\"><strong>Keyboard</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Move</td><td>Click open ground; a far click runs</td><td>Tap open ground</td><td>Arrow keys</td></tr><tr><td>Walk instead of run</td><td><strong>W</strong></td><td><strong>Walk</strong> button</td><td><strong>W</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Talk, use, open, search</td><td>Click the person or thing</td><td>Tap it</td><td><strong>E</strong> for the nearest; or <strong>T</strong>, then <strong>Enter</strong></td></tr><tr><td>See what you can use</td><td>Hold <strong>U</strong></td><td><strong>Labels</strong> button</td><td>Hold <strong>U</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Draw or sheathe your weapon</td><td><strong>Space</strong>, or the crossed swords</td><td>Crossed-swords button</td><td><strong>Space</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Attack</td><td>Click an enemy: you keep fighting him</td><td>Tap an enemy</td><td><strong>T</strong> to choose him, <strong>Enter</strong> to attack</td></tr><tr><td>Force an attack</td><td><strong>Shift</strong>+click</td><td>Tap <strong>Force</strong>, then the target</td><td><strong>Shift+Enter</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Choose an ability</td><td><strong>1–0</strong>, or <strong>S</strong> for the bar</td><td>Tap it in the ability bar</td><td><strong>1–0</strong>, or <strong>S</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Use the ability</td><td>Right-click the target, or open ground</td><td>Tap the target</td><td>The same number again</td></tr><tr><td>Pause</td><td><strong>P</strong>, or the <strong>Pause</strong> button</td><td><strong>Pause</strong> button</td><td><strong>P</strong> or Pause</td></tr><tr><td>Slow time; play one round</td><td><strong>V</strong>; <strong>N</strong> while paused</td><td><strong>Slow</strong>; <strong>Next round</strong></td><td><strong>V</strong>; <strong>N</strong> while paused</td></tr><tr><td>Control a companion</td><td>Click his portrait</td><td>Tap his portrait</td><td><strong>[</strong> and <strong>]</strong>; <strong>Home</strong> for yourself</td></tr><tr><td>Select squads (from IV)</td><td>Click a standard; <strong>Shift</strong>+click to add</td><td>Tap standards; <strong>Clear</strong> to finish</td><td><strong>Shift+1–6</strong> adds or removes</td></tr><tr><td>Order the selected squad</td><td>Right-click ground or an enemy</td><td>Tap ground or an enemy</td><td><strong>1–6</strong> on its command card; arrow keys and <strong>Enter</strong> to send it</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, character, journal</td><td><strong>I</strong>, <strong>C</strong>, <strong>J</strong></td><td>Menu buttons</td><td><strong>I</strong>, <strong>C</strong>, <strong>J</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Mission orders, chronicle, map</td><td><strong>Q</strong>, <strong>L</strong>, <strong>M</strong></td><td>Menu buttons</td><td><strong>Q</strong>, <strong>L</strong>, <strong>M</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Quick save</td><td><strong>F2</strong></td><td><strong>Menu → Save &amp; load → Quick save</strong></td><td><strong>F2</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Turn and zoom the 3D view</td><td>Middle-drag; scroll wheel</td><td>Two-finger twist; pinch</td><td><strong>,</strong> and <strong>.</strong>; <strong>+ / −</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Follow, overview, horizon</td><td><strong>F</strong>, <strong>Z</strong>, <strong>H</strong></td><td>Camera buttons</td><td><strong>F</strong>, <strong>Z</strong>, <strong>H</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Settings, help and saves</td><td><strong>Esc</strong> for the Menu; <strong>?</strong> for help</td><td><strong>Menu</strong> button</td><td><strong>Esc</strong>; <strong>?</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"help-note\"><p><strong>Tip</strong> Press <strong>P</strong> whenever a fight gets busy. While paused you can point at anything to read its forecast, choose abilities, pick targets and give orders; everyone carries out the latest command you gave him when you resume. The recruit drill starts paused so its timer waits for you.</p></aside>"
